language|communication-system|NOUN|System of human communication|A system of words or signs that people use to communicate.|ngôn ngữ; hệ thống từ hoặc ký hiệu để giao tiếp|The guide explained the rules in three languages.|Hướng dẫn viên giải thích các quy tắc bằng ba ngôn ngữ.|Language is countable for a particular system, such as a national language, and uncountable for communication in general.|language
sit|seated-position|VERB|Be in a seated position|Rest on a seat or another surface with the upper body upright, or move into that position.|ngồi; chuyển sang tư thế ngồi|We sat on the bench while the boat was being repaired.|Chúng tôi ngồi trên ghế dài trong lúc chiếc thuyền đang được sửa.|The forms are sit, sat, sat; sit down emphasizes moving into a seated position.|sit
stripe|coloured-band|NOUN|Band of contrasting colour|A long, narrow band whose colour differs from the surrounding surface.|sọc; dải màu khác với bề mặt xung quanh|A blue stripe runs along each sleeve of the jacket.|Một sọc xanh chạy dọc mỗi tay áo của chiếc áo khoác.|Stripe is countable; striped is the adjective for something marked with stripes.|stripe
horse|equine-animal|NOUN|Large animal used for riding|A large animal with hooves and a mane, often ridden or used to pull loads.|ngựa|The horse waited calmly while its rider adjusted the saddle.|Con ngựa bình tĩnh chờ trong lúc người cưỡi chỉnh yên.|Horse is countable; ride a horse names the activity and on horseback describes the means of travel.|horse
boy|male-child|NOUN|Male child or young person|A male child or young male person.|cậu bé; người nam còn trẻ|The boy carefully carried a tray of seedlings.|Cậu bé cẩn thận mang một khay cây con.|Boy is countable; boys is the regular plural. Context determines the person's age.|boy
astronaut|space-traveller|NOUN|Person trained for space travel|A person trained to travel and carry out work in space.|phi hành gia|The astronaut tested her equipment before the launch.|Nữ phi hành gia kiểm tra thiết bị của mình trước khi phóng.|Astronaut is countable and applies to people of any gender; an astronaut uses an because the word begins with a vowel sound.|astronaut
career|working-life|NOUN|Course of a person's working life|The course of someone's working life, including their jobs and professional development.|sự nghiệp; quá trình làm việc và phát triển nghề nghiệp|Anh changed direction halfway through his career.|Anh chuyển hướng giữa chặng đường sự nghiệp của mình.|Career is countable; a career in a field names the area of work and a career as a role names an occupation.|career
she|female-subject|PRONOUN|Female subject pronoun|Used as a subject to refer to a female person already known from the context.|cô ấy; chị ấy; bà ấy, dùng làm chủ ngữ|My aunt repairs bicycles, and she also teaches evening classes.|Dì tôi sửa xe đạp, và dì ấy cũng dạy các lớp buổi tối.|She is a third-person singular subject pronoun; use her as the object and choose Vietnamese address terms to fit the person.|she
vase|flower-container|NOUN|Container for flowers|A container used to hold and display cut flowers.|bình hoa; lọ cắm hoa|I placed a single sunflower in the glass vase.|Tôi cắm một bông hướng dương vào chiếc bình thủy tinh.|Vase is countable; a vase of flowers describes the container together with its flowers.|vase
because|reason-link|CONJUNCTION|Introduce a reason|Used to connect a statement with a clause that gives its reason.|bởi vì; vì, nối với mệnh đề chỉ lý do|We moved the picnic indoors because the wind was strong.|Chúng tôi chuyển buổi dã ngoại vào trong nhà vì gió mạnh.|Because takes a clause with a subject and verb; because of takes a noun phrase instead.|because
autumn|season|NOUN|Season after summer|The season that follows summer and comes before winter.|mùa thu|The village holds an apple festival each autumn.|Ngôi làng tổ chức lễ hội táo vào mỗi mùa thu.|Use in autumn or in the autumn; fall is the usual American English name for this season.|autumn
box|container|NOUN|Container for holding things|A container with a base and sides, usually a lid, used to store or carry things.|hộp; vật chứa đồ có đáy và thành|The mechanic kept spare screws in a metal box.|Người thợ máy cất những con vít dự phòng trong một hộp kim loại.|Box is countable, with plural boxes; a box of something names its contents.|box
semester|academic-period|NOUN|Main part of an academic year|One of the main teaching periods into which an academic year is divided, usually two.|học kỳ|This semester, our class is studying local history.|Học kỳ này, lớp chúng tôi đang học lịch sử địa phương.|Semester is countable; this semester needs no preposition when used as a time expression.|semester
exam|knowledge-test|NOUN|Formal test|A formal test used to assess someone's knowledge or ability.|bài thi; kỳ thi đánh giá kiến thức hoặc năng lực|The students checked their answers before the exam ended.|Các học sinh kiểm tra đáp án của mình trước khi bài thi kết thúc.|Exam is countable; take an exam means sit the test, while pass an exam means achieve a successful result.|exam
everybody|all-people|PRONOUN|All people in a group|Every person in the group relevant to the situation.|mọi người; tất cả người trong nhóm đang được nói đến|Everybody has a turn to speak at our class meeting.|Mọi người đều có lượt phát biểu trong cuộc họp lớp của chúng tôi.|Everybody takes a singular verb, such as has; they can refer back to everybody when gender is unspecified.|everybody
dolphin|aquatic-mammal|NOUN|Aquatic mammal|An aquatic mammal with a streamlined body that breathes air and usually has a beaklike snout.|cá heo; động vật có vú sống dưới nước|A dolphin surfaced beside the fishing boat.|Một con cá heo nổi lên mặt nước bên cạnh thuyền đánh cá.|Dolphin is countable; although the Vietnamese name contains cá, dolphins are mammals rather than fish.|dolphin
breakfast|morning-meal|NOUN|First meal of the day|The first meal of the day, normally eaten in the morning.|bữa sáng; bữa ăn đầu ngày|We shared a breakfast of rice porridge before the journey.|Chúng tôi cùng ăn một bữa sáng gồm cháo trước chuyến đi.|Have breakfast usually has no article; a breakfast can identify a particular meal or type of breakfast.|breakfast
excited|enthusiastic-feeling|ADJECTIVE|Feeling eager and enthusiastic|Feeling eager and enthusiastic about something that is happening or expected.|hào hứng; phấn khích|Bao was excited about showing his model bridge to the class.|Bảo hào hứng về việc giới thiệu mô hình cây cầu của mình với cả lớp.|Use excited about a noun or -ing form, or excited to do; exciting describes the cause of the feeling.|excited
tornado|rotating-air-column|NOUN|Violently rotating air column|A violently rotating column of air that extends from a storm cloud to the ground.|lốc xoáy|The tornado damaged several empty farm buildings.|Cơn lốc xoáy làm hư hại một số công trình nông trại đang trống.|Tornado is countable; tornadoes is a common plural form. Use it for the weather phenomenon rather than an ordinary gust.|tornado
clothes|body-garments|NOUN|Garments worn on the body|Items such as shirts and trousers that people wear to cover their bodies.|quần áo; đồ mặc|She folded the clean clothes and put them in a drawer.|Cô ấy gấp quần áo sạch rồi cất chúng vào một ngăn kéo.|Clothes is a plural noun and takes a plural verb; use an item of clothing to count one piece.|clothes
